<%# Saccade, 2026-11-21: the sign-in code e-mail laid out like the usual one-time-code e-mails (code on its own line, large),
    so mail apps recognise the code (Gmail "Copy code", iPhone/Mac code autofill). The subject with the code and the
    Auto-Submitted header come from config/initializers/saccade_otp_email.rb. Locals: code, name (document).
    Modification of DocuSeal 3.3.8 (AGPL-3.0); source: https://github.com/warlock9k00/docuseal-saccade. %>
<div style="max-width:480px;padding:8px 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252D;line-height:1.5">
  <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:15px">Your verification code is:</p>
  <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:32px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:6px;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace"><%= code %></p>
  <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:15px">Enter this code to open &ldquo;<%= name %>&rdquo;. It is valid for up to 10 minutes.</p>
  <p style="margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#6B6470">Didn&rsquo;t request this code? Ignore this e-mail or reply to let us know.</p>
</div>
